---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Help with downloads, copying and tools | 88cutouts" description="Fix failed clipboard copies, find downloaded PNGs, understand transparency, and save your collage before closing the browser.">
  <div class="wrap"><article class="prose">
    <h1>Downloads and tool help</h1>
    <h2>Copy does not work</h2>
    <p>Image clipboard support varies by browser and destination app. Open the page in your normal browser rather than a social app's embedded browser and tap Copy again. If permission is denied or the destination will not paste an image, use Download. See the <a href="/blog/copy-image-to-clipboard-guide/">clipboard guide</a>.</p>
    <h2>Where did my download go?</h2>
    <p>Check your browser's downloads list or your device's Files or Downloads folder. A PNG saved as a file may not automatically appear in the Photos gallery. Open the file and use the device's share or save controls if you need it there.</p>
    <h2>A white or grey box appears</h2>
    <p>A preview app may show transparency on a solid background. Test the file over a coloured layer in an image editor. A screenshot or JPEG conversion removes transparency; download the original PNG instead. Read <a href="/blog/check-png-transparency/">how to test the alpha channel</a>.</p>
    <h2>The sticker looks too small or blurry</h2>
    <p>Check both file dimensions and artwork dimensions on its page. Transparent margins can make a large file contain a small visible subject. Reduce its display size, or trim the margin in an editor; cropping does not add detail. See <a href="/blog/transparent-padding-sticker-size/">the margin example</a>.</p>
    <h2>Save a composition</h2>
    <p>Download your result before refreshing or closing the <a href="/collage-maker/">collage maker</a> or <a href="/ransom-note/">cutout text maker</a>. Tools run locally in your browser; there is no account recovery or saved-project service.</p>
    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a> with the page address, device, browser and what happened. Please do not send passwords or private photos. Rights and licensing enquiries are covered on <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
